        <item>
            <title>0.8.11</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:06:33 +1200</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>22</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.8.11</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}.rn{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,"SF Pro Text",sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:4px 2px}.rn h1{font-size:16px;margin:0 0 10px}.rn h2{font-size:14px;margin:14px 0 6px}.rn ul{margin:6px 0;padding-left:20px}.rn li{margin-bottom:7px}.rn code{font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12px}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.rn{color:#e8e8ed}}</style><div class="rn"><h1>Rein 0.8.11</h1>
<ul>
<li><b>Rein Remote reconnects reliably.</b> A network blip could send the Mac's relay connection into a</li>
</ul>
<p>  silent churn loop — the iPhone app then searched for the Mac forever. The connection layer now</p>
<p>  recovers from drops cleanly, and both apps detect a "zombie" link (connected in name only) within</p>
<p>  seconds and rejoin on their own. After updating, open Rein's window, pick <b>Remote</b> in the sidebar,</p>
<p>  and tap <b>Redeploy</b> once so your relay picks up the matching server-side fix.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Hidden menu bar icons stay hidden.</b> Icons tucked behind the ⋮ divider could reappear after the</li>
</ul>
<p>  display slept, a monitor was plugged in, or the screen resolution changed — and on wider displays</p>
<p>  the reveal chevron itself could vanish into the hidden section. The hidden section now re-asserts</p>
<p>  itself after every such event, sizes itself to your actual displays, and self-repairs if macOS</p>
<p>  shuffles the controls out of order.</p></div>
]]></description>
